    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59e278d3_7b89c2fb",
        "filename": "android/pandora/server/proto/pandora/gatt.proto",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1880948
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-18T18:12:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not an overlap.\nThe GATT MMIs work differently than the ones in A2DP or HFP and can\u0027t be handled the same.\nWhen when calling createBond, the pts-bot will call the \"confirm passkey\" MMI so we have to have answered the connect MMI beforehand. Only when we confirmed the passkey and returned we will be able to call connectGatt so it has to be done asynchronously.",
      "parentUuid": "b2872b41_48f97184",
      "revId": "669a5cbf8f1f794f780ea53985ebf89a3b0ff1d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd1d86e7_524bc381",
        "filename": "android/pandora/server/proto/pandora/gatt.proto",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-19T13:42:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t need to something when the PTS asks it, it is a correct and I would say even preferred implementation for us to do the confirm passkey as part of the connect and just do nothing when the pts will ask to \"confirm passkey\" as this is either already done or this will be triggered by the connection.\n\nThe MMIs are just a hint on what the PTS expects as long as we do what is wanted and the test pass we are free to implement that how we want.",
      "parentUuid": "59e278d3_7b89c2fb",
      "revId": "669a5cbf8f1f794f780ea53985ebf89a3b0ff1d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
